title Caravan overtake -- a document that names its regions has already named its lawful order
prompt Autonomous loop -- take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the Microkernel Target double-seat, Standfast on reds first, one council-rota doc deep-read, condense REMEMBER, send the finished increment.
think Standfast first. Walked crux/REDS.md end to end -- living rows 80, 83, 84, 85 and the prose notes for 81, 82, 85-reopened, 86, and 87 each carry a closure with a witness on metal, so no agent-closable red stands open and the constructive queue is clear.
think The running thread is the last lap's recommend line, and it named the crux exactly -- whether a supervisor may look past a blocked head at all, and what a document would have to declare for reordering to stay meaning-preserving rather than merely faster.
think Council rota by lap index -- 468 .kyri logs on disk, this is lap 469, and 469 mod 27 = 10, so the deep-read was foundations/20260703-182612_sameness-is-the-macro.md. Its teaching shaped the answer rather than decorating it: compress by making things publicly similar, and refuse the compression that needs a private dialect. A new word in the declaration would have been exactly that private dialect -- so the rung asked whether the document already said enough, and it did.
think The answer turns on separating two questions the rungs before it had reason to hold together. Whether two items may run at the same instant is a question about domains, and rolling.admissible answers it -- a domain never stands beside itself. Whether one item may run before another is a question about regions alone, and the module's own share_a_hop answers that one without asking which domain anything belongs to.
think That separation is where the room is. Two items of one domain may not run at once, yet an item of another domain touching none of their regions may pass them freely, and no rung before this one could say so because no rung before this one had reason to ask the finer question.
think The measure had to get finer too. Rolling counts a turn where a fill admitted nobody, which reads a turn that admitted one child of three as busy. This rung adds slots_unspent -- free slots summed over every turn that still had work waiting -- and keeps the coarse count beside it, so the two rungs stay comparable while the finer one carries the finding.
think The queue stops being a line once an item may enter from behind the head, so the table carries which items are taken and the head is simply the first that is not. The look past the head is bounded twice -- at most max_lookahead items still waiting, and never past the end of the queue -- so a supervisor spends its turn running rather than deciding.
think Reuse over restatement, two ways. rolling.admissible was already open from the harvest lap and is asked rather than restated; rolling.ordered_queue opened pub this lap so the question is put to the very lap that rung measured rather than to a copy of it.
obs The finding came in two halves again, and the shape rhymes with harvest without repeating it. Over the ordered lap overtaking converts nothing -- zero lawful passes, the same nine slot-turns unspent under both readings, six asks home either way -- because every candidate is refused either by the running table, the virtualiser touching all three clients, or by a region it shares with the head. Over a lap whose head blocks on its own domain it converts the whole of it: two slot-turns unspent in line against zero, two lawful passes reaching two items back, same four children and same peak of three.
obs The unchecked control is the meaning-preservation proof and it broke on metal rather than in argument. It keeps the isolation exactly and drops only the order test; handed a lap where a taker sits behind its own passer, it takes first, the home hears no bell that was never rung, and the run refuses with OutcomeMismatch. Faster and wrong, measured.
obs The stronger probe reaches further. Drop the order test from the checked reading and the ordered lap itself refuses -- so that lap's zero lawful passes is real work the test is doing, never an absence of candidates to refuse. The second probe removes overtaking entirely and the self-blocking lap reds at two slot-turns unspent. Both RED paths proven before the green was claimed.
obs Twenty-nine green-witnessed Rye rings now carry the Microkit shape across real processes. TAME surface GREEN -- style bans clean, width-check exit 0 -- and the neighbors this lap touched all re-GREEN: rolling, harvest, cohort.
loom witness=caravan_overtake ordered_slots_line=9 ordered_slots_pass=9 ordered_passes=0 homed=6 peak_in_flight=3
loom witness=caravan_overtake block_slots_line=2 block_slots_pass=0 passes=2 pass_reach=2 children=4
file caravan/overtake.rye the rung -- three readings of one queue, differing only in whether and how a blocked head may be passed, with the order test derived from the declaration's own regions
file tools/caravan_overtake_witness.rish the witness on metal -- both halves of the finding and the unchecked control checked natively
file caravan/rolling.rye ordered_queue opened pub, so the question is asked of the very lap that rung measured
file caravan/README.md the overtake section and roster row -- the doc moves in the same commit as the behavior it describes
file crux/REMEMBER.md live edge refreshed to this rung, the harvest edge condensed into the prior-edges line
recommend keep-going the honest next crux is what the order test cannot see -- it reads the regions an item names and nothing about what the item does to them, so a reader and a writer of one region read as equally ordered when only one direction is real, and the question becomes whether a document's grants already say enough to tell a pair that must keep its order from a pair that merely touches the same bytes
